<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mas'ud III of Ghazni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1099–1115</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mas'ud III was a sultan of the Ghaznavid dynasty who reigned from 1099 to 1115, succeeding his father Ibrahim. His reign was a period of relative peace and prosperity, with campaigns into northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and a stable frontier with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a>, to whom the Ghaznavids were linked by marriage. Building works at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazni">Ghazni</a>, including a palace, date from his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/masud-iii-of-ghazni.jpg" alt="Mas'ud III of Ghazni" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M.samei · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mas%27ud_III_Gold_Dinar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
